      "text": "The given equation of the ellipse is in the form \\((x - h)^2 / a^2 + (y - k)^2 / b^2 = 1\\), where the center of the ellipse is \\((h, k) = (1, 1)\\), \\(a^2 = 36\\) (since \\(b^2 = 25\\)), and \\(b^2 = 25\\). Therefore, \\(a = 6\\) and \\(b = 5\\).\n\nFor an ellipse, the distance from the center to each focus is given by \\(c = \\sqrt{a^2 - b^2}\\). Substituting the values of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\):\n\n\\[ c = \\sqrt{36 - 25} = \\sqrt{11} \\]\n\nThe foci of the ellipse are located at \\((h \\pm c, k)\\). Therefore, the foci are at \\((1 + \\sqrt{11}, 1)\\) and \\((1 - \\sqrt{11}, 1)\\). The distance between the foci is the distance between these two points:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\sqrt{((1 + \\sqrt{11}) - (1 - \\sqrt{11}))^2 + (1 - 1)^2} = \\sqrt{(2\\sqrt{11})^2} = \\sqrt{44} = 2\\sqrt{11} \\]\n\nThus, the distance between the foci is \\(\\boxed{2\\sqrt{11}}\\).",
